{
  "manufacturer": "Danfoss",
  "manufacturer_slug": "danfoss",
  "model": "VLT Compressor Drive CDS 803 (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "cds-803",
  "short_model": "CDS 803",
  "aliases": [
    "CDS803",
    "CDS-803",
    "VLT Compressor Drive CDS 803"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "VLT Compressor Drive CDS 803 (variable-speed compressor drive for HVAC/R) using the built-in RS-485 port with 8-30 Protocol = Modbus RTU; Modbus rules from Design Guide MG18N202 (software 1.20), parameter data from Programming Guide MG18P202 (software 2.0).",
  "summary": "Danfoss's drive for variable-speed refrigeration and air-conditioning compressors. Its RS-485 port runs Modbus RTU: the FC-profile control and status words are coils 1-16 and 33-48, and every parameter is a holding register at ten times its parameter number. This map covers the control/status coils, compressor readouts, fault and warning words, and the communication and timeout parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "parameter-derived",
    "note": "The design guide states coil 1 is sent as 0000 and holding register 40001 as 0000. A parameter's register is 10 x its parameter number (3-03 -> 3030), sent minus 1: the guide's example reads 3-03 at start address 0x0BD5 (3029). Coils are 1-based too (coil 65 is sent as 64)."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "Design guide software 1.20; programming guide software 2.0",
  "source": {
    "title": "VLT Compressor Drive CDS 803 Design Guide (chapter 7 RS485 Installation and Set-up)",
    "doc_number": "MG18N202",
    "revision_date": "2015-12",
    "url": "https://files.danfoss.com/download/Drives/MG18N202.pdf",
    "pages": "Design Guide pp. 58-64 (coil and register addressing, coil table 7.15, CTW table 7.16, STW table 7.17, register table, parameter handling and read example 3-03 = 0016E360h pp. 63-64), FC profile pp. 64-67. Programming Guide MG18P202 (06/2019) parameter lists pp. 76-86 (conversion index and data type), 8-0*/8-3* descriptions pp. 37-39."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Parameter data (conversion index, data type) come from VLT Compressor Drive CDS 803 Programming Guide MG18P202, https://files.danfoss.com/download/Drives/MG18P202.pdf. Scale = 10^conversion index; the hour counters carry index 74 (factor 3600, i.e. hours expressed in seconds), so one count is one hour.",
    "32-bit values are high word first: the design guide reads 3-03 at registers 3030/3031 and gets 0016 E360 hex = 1500000 (1500.000 with conversion index -3).",
    "8-bit parameters (Uint8) are read and written as one 16-bit register. 16-34 Heatsink Temp (Int8) is left out because the sign extension in the 16-bit register is not stated.",
    "Coils 17-32 (speed reference) and 49-64 (output frequency / feedback) carry 16-bit words bit by bit; they are not listed. REF/MAV use 4000 hex = 100 % of the reference range (two's complement for negative).",
    "Alarm, warning and extended status words (16-90..16-94) are listed as raw UINT32; bit meanings are in the programming guide.",
    "The two guides cover different software versions (1.20 and 2.0); check 15-43 Software Version on site."
  ],
